collaboration: Wake parents for child results

A finished MultiAgentV2 child previously queued its terminal result
without starting an idle parent turn.
The parent could remain idle or unload before consuming the result.

Make terminal results request a parent turn.
Keep each live child's ancestor chain resident until the recipient
mailbox accepts the handoff.
Transfer each triggering delivery's ancestor lease into the recipient
mailbox, then into the turn that drains it.
Keep the finishing child's execution slot through terminal acceptance.
Recheck idle unload eligibility in the session submission queue so an
accepted wake cannot be discarded by an earlier idle observation.
During terminal session teardown, discard queued mailbox work instead
of starting a successor turn.
Keep app-server teardown ownership until an accepted shutdown finishes.

Keep passive agent messages queue-only.
